summary.label:
Diseases Dictionary Offline is complete OFFLINE and FREE app containing list of Medical disorders & diseases that provides all information about symptoms, disorder and treatment and many medical terminology.
This Diseases & Disorders Dictionary hand book can act as a clinical advisor for self diagnosis and can also be used to look up symptoms, diseases and treatment. Medical dictionary free download is like a FREE Doctor at home for common diseases and treatment codes.

Diseases Dictionary - Medical App Features:
1. Offline – It wok offline, no active internet connection is required;
2. Detailed description of all major medical conditions and diseases: 
- definition;
- symptoms;
- causes;
- risk factors;
- complications;
- preparing for your appointment;
- tests and diagnosis;
- treatments and drugs;
- lifestyle and home remedies

3. Easily find needed disease with instant search.
4. Favorites list– you are able to bookmark the Disease item to your favorites list by clicking on the “star” icon.

Who can use this dictionary:
Healthcare professionals, pharmaceuticals, physicians, hospital nurses, medical students, nursing professionals, pharmacy, physician assistants and for students who work in clinical practice & dispensary.

※ Find the pharmacological classification of any medicine in seconds by simply searching for the medicine name or brand.

※Find alternative medicines within the same class. An essential resource during drug shortages and also for finding clinical equivalents.

※ Reinforce your medicine knowledge with a medicine classification test and structure activity.


FOR HEALTHCARE PROFESSIONALS:

※ Quickly find alternative therapies by pharmacological class - essential during drug shortages.

※ Having trouble remembering alpha-2 adrenergic agonists and alpha-1 antagonists? The personalized pharmacological index will help you find medications by class quickly and help with terminologies you need to know in your daily practices;

※ Layout similar to medication leaflets: An ideal application for clinical texts such as British National Formulary (BNF) and United States National Formulary (USNF);

※ Stay up to date with the latest drug technologies approved by the FDA and EMA(Europe) until 2024;


FOR HEALTH STUDENTS:

※ Pharmacology tool for health and general science courses;

※ Companion app for pharmacology and medicinal chemistry textbooks;


FOR REFERENCE:

※ Pharmacological Index - Designed exclusively for Pharmacodex by a PhD pharmacist, covering 15 systems and over 2,000 pharmacological sub-classifications;

※Pharmaceutical Search - The Index's full search capacity allows you to find equivalent drugs by pharmacological class - essential during drug shortages to quickly find clinical alternatives;

※Bookmarks - Create bookmarks and notes for each medicine to review later;

※ Filters - Substances can be filtered by Pharmaceutical, Nutritional and Phytotherapeutic type;

※ References - Direct links to FDA, EMA, PubChem, PubMed, DailyMed, EMC and etc to quickly find prescription information from reliable and up-to-date sources;


FOR LEARNING:

※ Pharmacology - Strengthen the pharmacological classification of medicines;

※ Medicinal Chemistry - Strengthen Structure-Activity Relationships (SARs) through the identification of structures;

※ Practice classifying medicines and identifying structures for a few minutes a day - A little regular practice has been proven to improve recall and reinforce learning;

※ Monitor your learning progression across 15 systems and over 2,000 pharmacological sub-classifications. Review previous test results to reinforce memory;

※ Not sure about any pharmacological classification? - Artificial Intelligence integrated into the App will help you explain all pharmacological and chemical terms;

※ If you want to focus on a specific pharmacological class, you can create your own custom drug structure/classification questionnaire in seconds - choose from 15 systems and over 2,000 pharmacological classifications, including infectious diseases, cancers, genetic and metabolic disorders;



This is your ideal companion app for understanding and mastering drug leaflets and pharmacology textbooks. The App allows quick consultation to find equivalent medications by pharmacological class. It is ideal to help develop and reinforce the fundamentals of pharmacology and medicinal chemistry, an essential resource in day-to-day clinical decision-making.
